<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I actually noticed what this person is going through, or only what their trouble costs me?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I acting to ease their suffering, or to escape my own discomfort at seeing it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is my concern shaded by a quiet judgement that they brought this on themselves, or that I am above them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would I feel and act the same way if the people suffering were many, distant or unlike me?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I stop and take it in: 'That's a hard week. What would help most right now?' I move the deadline with the client myself, ask whether they want work taken off them or kept as a distraction, and agree a check-in for next week so the rest of the team isn't left guessing." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I either brush past it ('sorry to hear that, but the client is furious, I need it by tomorrow') or I am so upset for them that I quietly redo the work myself at midnight and never mention the deadline again." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A reliable team member misses a client deadline and, when you ask about it, mentions that a parent was taken into hospital last week." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Compassion notices the suffering and is moved by it, but it also stays steady enough to choose help that fits this person and stays fair to everyone else involved." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Virtue> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Compassion" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ceyin (commiseration)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "compassionate concern" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "karuṇā" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The settled disposition to notice another's suffering, be moved by it without being overwhelmed, and want and act to relieve it, steered by judgement about what will actually help." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/compassion-and-relationships> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Compassion" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassionate-reappraisal> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy> .
