<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did the person actually ask for my advice, or am I volunteering it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do I understand their situation and constraints, or am I answering the problem I once had?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I explained my reasoning, so they can judge it rather than just obey it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I giving this advice for their sake, or because being the one who knows feels good?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If they decide differently, can I let it go?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Congratulations. Before I say what I think, what's making you hesitate? … It sounds as if the worry is managing two close friends. I'm not you, so take this as one view: when I faced that, what helped was talking to them early. Who else knows this team well that you could ask?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Take it. I did exactly the same thing and it was the best move I ever made. You'll regret it forever if you say no." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A colleague stops by your desk and says she has been offered a promotion to manage her current team, but isn't sure she wants it. You once took a similar step and loved it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "The wiser response listens first, finds out what the real question is, offers a view as one perspective with its reasoning shown, and leaves the decision with the person who has to live with it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Context> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Giving advice" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "advice giving" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "advising others" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "being asked for advice" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "giving counsel" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "offering advice" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/social-relationships> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The situation of being asked, or feeling moved, to tell someone else what they should do about a problem in their life or work — a test of wisdom that psychologists have used to measure it, and one where good intentions often go wrong." .
