<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If our positions were reversed, would I accept being treated the way I'm about to treat this person?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I applying my own tastes, or the underlying respect I'd want, and have I asked what they actually want?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would I be comfortable if everyone in my position acted on the reason I'm acting on now?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does this relationship's difference in power change what treating them as an equal would require?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "What I'd want is to have my effort noticed and valued. I'll ask her how she likes to be recognised; she prefers a note to her director and first pick of the next project, so that is what she gets." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I'd love to be praised in front of the whole department, so I'll call her up at the all-hands and give a big speech." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A manager wants to thank a quiet, highly reliable analyst for rescuing a delayed project." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "The manager keeps the rule's core (give the respect and appreciation you'd want) but stops projecting a personal taste onto someone who doesn't share it, which is the most common way the rule misfires." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Principle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Golden Rule" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "do unto others" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "ethic of reciprocity" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "reciprocity (Confucian)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "shu" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "silver rule" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "恕" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-principles> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The widely shared moral maxim to treat others as you would want to be treated, in a positive form (\"do to others what you would have them do to you\") or a negative one (\"do not do to others what you would not want done to you\"); best read as a habit of imaginative fairness, checked against what the other person actually wants." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/compassion-and-relationships> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Golden Rule" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/analects> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/compassion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/confucianism> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/impartial-spectator> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/golden-rule> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/golden-rule/s1> .
