  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "keeping a poker face" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "stiff upper lip" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "suppressing emotions" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotion-regulation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Habitually hiding the outward signs of a feeling (face, voice, posture) once it is already under way, instead of changing how the situation is understood; it calms the surface without calming the feeling, and as a default habit it tends to cost memory, closeness and well-being." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/emotional-suppression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/emotions-and-equanimity> .
