<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do I actually have the specific knowledge or skill this action needs, or am I borrowing confidence from success somewhere else?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Whose interests, besides mine, does this decision affect, and how will it look in a year rather than this week?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I assuming the consequences won't reach me because of my position, record or cleverness?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When someone questioned this plan, did I answer their point or just wave it away?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "\"Fair question. My experience is with the old schema, not this one, so I don't actually know. Let's run it against the staging copy and ship on Monday, when people are around if it goes wrong.\" The test exposes a locking problem, which is fixed before release." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "\"I've done this kind of change a hundred times. Testing it would take all afternoon, and nothing is going to break.\" The change goes out unreviewed, fails over the weekend, and the on-call staff spend two days repairing it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A senior engineer, the most experienced person on the team, wants to push a database change to the live system late on a Friday. A junior colleague asks whether it has been tested against a copy of the real data." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Expertise in one area tempts people to feel knowledgeable and safe everywhere; asking what this particular action requires, who bears the cost if it fails, and whether a dissenting question has been answered brings confidence back into line with what is actually known." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Vice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Folly" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "foolish behaviour" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "foolishness" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "low levels of wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "the fool" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "unwise behaviour" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/poor-judgment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The practical opposite of wisdom: acting with more confidence than one's knowledge, self-knowledge or self-control warrants, and ignoring others' interests and long-term consequences. Psychologists stress that folly is not the same as low intelligence; bright, successful people are often especially prone to it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/foundations> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Folly" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/robert-sternberg> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/folly> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning> .
