  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I know the code well, but not the customers' timelines or the budget. Let me lay out what I'm sure of and what I'm guessing, ask sales and finance what I'm missing, and recommend the option that serves the people who depend on this, not the one I'd enjoy." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I know this codebase better than anyone, so the answer is obviously a rewrite. No need to hear the others." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A team member with deep technical knowledge is asked whether the team should rebuild a struggling product from scratch or keep repairing it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Expertise is not yet wisdom; the wiser answer knows the limits of its own knowledge, takes other perspectives in, and aims at the good of everyone affected." .
