  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "the wise person" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Doing well, in thought and in action, with respect to how to live: knowing or reasonably believing what matters, seeing the limits of what one knows, and using that understanding to judge, advise and act well. Philosophers debate its exact conditions; psychologists describe it as morally grounded metacognition applied to real problems." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/foundations> .
