<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I decide what \"good enough\" means before I started comparing, or am I letting each new option move the target?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is this choice important and hard to undo enough to justify searching for the best, or would a good option serve just as well?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I set a limit on how many options or how much time I will spend?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Now that I have chosen, am I still checking what I gave up or what others picked?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "We need four things: our existing workflows, a single sign-on, an export option and a price under our budget. I'll trial tools from the shortlist IT already approved, adopt the first one that meets all four, and stop shopping once it's in." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I'll trial every serious tool on the market, build a forty-row comparison sheet and keep reading reviews until I'm sure we have the best one." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead has to replace the team's project-tracking tool within a month, and dozens of products are available." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Fixing the standard before searching turns an endless comparison into a bounded task, and stopping after the choice spares the team the second-guessing that research links to looking for the best." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Before you look at any options, write down the few things the choice must achieve and the minimum each must reach; this is your \"good enough\" line." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Decide in advance how much search the choice deserves, such as a number of options, a deadline or a budget of hours, scaled to how much is at stake and how reversible it is." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Look at options one at a time and take the first that clears every line, rather than collecting the whole field to rank." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "If nothing clears the line within your search budget, lower one standard deliberately; if many options clear it at once, raise one, and say which and why." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Once you have chosen, stop comparing; do not keep checking the options you passed up or what others chose." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Keep maximizing-style search for the rare choices where a better option is worth the extra effort and the decision is hard to undo." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Satisficing" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Practice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Satisficing" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "aspiration-level choice" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "good-enough choosing" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "satisficer decision strategy" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/bounded-rationality> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Choosing by first deciding what would count as good enough, then searching only until an option meets that standard, instead of trying to find and confirm the single best option." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/judgment-and-decisions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Satisficing" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/fast-and-frugal-heuristics> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/major-life-decision> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-algebra> .
