<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would going without this actually cause me pain, or would I just feel I had fallen behind someone?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Does this desire have a natural stopping point, or would more always seem better?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What am I already giving up, in time, health or peace, to chase it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Which of these would actually hurt to go without? We need more space for the kids, so that's real. The car and the title are mostly about how I look next to others, and I can drop them if they cost my evenings." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Everyone at my level has these things. Once I have them I'll finally be able to relax." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "After a good year, a project manager starts eyeing a bigger house, a premium car and a more senior title, and finds herself working weekends and sleeping badly to get all three." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Sorting the wants separates a real need from desires driven by comparison, so effort goes where it buys security and the rest stops dictating her time." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Principle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Classification of desires" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Epicurean classification of desires" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Principal Doctrine 29" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "empty desires" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "natural and necessary desires" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "vain desires" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/epicurean-ethics> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Epicurus's teaching that desires are natural and necessary, natural but unnecessary, or empty (born of groundless opinion), and that a good life comes from meeting the first, enjoying the second lightly, and seeing through the third, whose objects can never be had in full." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/classification-of-desires> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/meaning-and-the-good-life> .
