<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If nothing changed tomorrow, would my life be enough, and what exactly would be missing?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is this want mine, or did a comparison or an advert just switch it on?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I confused being content with giving up on something that genuinely needs fixing?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When I last got what I wanted, how long did the satisfaction actually last?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Is anything about my work actually worse than it was yesterday? If there's something I really want, like the scope or the pay, I'll go after that on purpose. If not, I'll let the comparison pass." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I need to start interviewing elsewhere this week; I can't be the one who got left behind." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A colleague in a similar role announces a promotion and a bigger title, and your own job, which you liked yesterday, suddenly feels small." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Contentment separates a real, specific need from wanting that was switched on by comparison; it keeps ambition but stops it from setting the price of one's peace." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Virtue> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Contentment" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "being content with little" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "knowing what is enough" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "santutthi" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "santuṭṭhi" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/well-being> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The settled sense that one's present life is sufficient and complete as it is, together with the habit of not letting limitless wanting set the terms of one's peace; a quiet, low-arousal good rather than an excited one." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/meaning-and-the-good-life> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Contentment" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/acceptance> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/equanimity> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/gratitude> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-adaptation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/satisficing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/simplicity> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/contentment/s1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/contentment/s2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/contentment/s3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/contentment/s4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/contentment/s5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/contentment/s6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#addresses> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/greed> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/contentment> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#contrastsWith> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/happiness> .
