<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I treating enjoyment as frivolous, or meaning as a duty, rather than letting each do its own work in my life?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When I judge whether a choice will make me better off, am I thinking only about how it will feel this week, or also about whether it fits what I value and want to grow into?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I relying on a neat label (pleasure versus meaning) where my actual experience is more mixed?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I'll do one thing purely for enjoyment, like a long lunch with friends, and one thing I care about, like finishing the bookshelf I'm building with my kid, and see how each leaves me feeling on Monday and a month from now." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Pleasure is shallow; I'll spend the weekend on a self-improvement course so the time counts for something." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "After a draining quarter, a team lead plans a free weekend and wonders how to spend it to feel restored." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Research suggests pleasure-seeking and meaning-seeking pay off on different timescales and work best together, so treating one as the \"real\" happiness tends to shortchange the other." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Framework> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hedonic and eudaimonic well-being" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "hedonia and eudaimonia" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "hedonia versus eudaimonia" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "hedonic-eudaimonic distinction" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "pleasure versus meaning" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "subjective versus psychological well-being" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/well-being> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The widely used framework in well-being research that separates hedonic well-being (pleasure, positive mood and life satisfaction) from eudaimonic well-being (meaning, growth, excellence and living by one's values); useful for reflecting on how one lives, but contested as a scientific division because self-report measures of the two overlap almost completely." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/meaning-and-the-good-life> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hedonic-and-eudaimonic-well-being> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Hedonic and eudaimonic well-being" .
