  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/ikigai> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An everyday Japanese word for what makes life feel worth living, and for the felt sense of having it; research treats it as close to eudaimonic well-being. The popular Western \"ikigai\" Venn diagram of passion, skill, need and pay is a recent business-coaching overlay, not the Japanese concept, and claims that ikigai lengthens life outrun the observational evidence." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/ikigai> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/meaning-and-the-good-life> .
