  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Logotherapy" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Frankl's logotherapy" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Logotherapie" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "logotherapy and existential analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "third Viennese school of psychotherapy" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/existential-psychotherapy> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Viktor Frankl's meaning-centred approach to psychotherapy and to life, which holds that the search for meaning is a basic human motive and that meaning can be found through what we create, what and whom we experience, and the attitude we take toward suffering we cannot avoid." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/logotherapy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/meaning-and-the-good-life> .
