<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is what feels missing right now coherence, direction, or a sense that this is worth doing?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I treating a bad week or a low mood as a verdict on my whole life?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would I still judge this pursuit worthwhile if I stopped feeling drawn to it, and would I still care about it if no one else valued it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Which part is missing: does the work no longer make sense to me, have I lost direction, or do I doubt it is worth doing? Let me fix the piece I can, starting with who actually relies on what I do." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "None of this matters, so I'll stop caring, coast, and wait until I feel inspired to find my calling." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "After a reorganisation, an analyst's work is folded into another team and she starts to feel that her job, and her weeks, no longer add up to anything." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Splitting meaning into coherence, purpose and significance turns a vague sense of emptiness into a specific, workable question, and meaning tends to follow connection and contribution rather than waiting for a revelation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Concept> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Meaning in life" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "life meaning" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "meaningful life" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "meaningfulness" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "presence of meaning" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "sense of meaning" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/well-being> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The sense that one's life makes sense, has direction and matters: in psychology, a judgment with three facets (coherence, purpose and significance); in philosophy, the question of what, beyond happiness and morality, makes an individual life worthwhile." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/meaning-in-life> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/meaning-and-the-good-life> .
