<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Whose interests have I left off the list, including people who are not in the room?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would this choice still look good to me a year from now, not just this week?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I adapting, trying to change things, or walking away, and is that the right response here?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is the common good I am appealing to one the other people affected would recognise, or just my own preference dressed up?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I want this project, the junior colleague needs support, and the client needs the deliverable. Can I ask for a one-week start date, pair them with a senior for three days, and take the project after?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "This is my shot. Take the project, reassign the work tonight and let the junior person sort themselves out." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead is offered a high-profile project that would mean handing a struggling junior colleague's half-finished work to someone else three days before the client deadline." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "The first answer serves only one interest in the short term; the second looks for an option that balances personal, interpersonal and wider interests over a longer horizon, which is what Sternberg means by a wise solution." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Name the decision and the outcome you are tempted to choose before you start weighing it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "List the interests at stake on three levels - yours, those of the specific people around you, and those of the wider team, community or environment." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "For each option, write down who gains and who pays in the next few weeks and in a few years." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask whether to adapt to the situation, try to change it, or leave it for a better one, and why." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Choose the option that best serves a common good you could defend out loud to everyone affected, and say which value settled the trade-off." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Balance theory of wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Framework> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Balance theory of wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Sternberg's balance theory of wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "augmented balance theory of wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "balance theory" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/psychology-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Robert Sternberg's model of wisdom as the use of intelligence, creativity, knowledge and experience, guided by positive ethical values, to reach a common good by balancing one's own, other people's and wider interests over the short and long term, and by choosing well among adapting to a situation, reshaping it or leaving it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/science-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Balance theory of wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/berlin-wisdom-paradigm> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/common-wisdom-model> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/implicit-theories-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/knowing-when-to-quit> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/practical-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/teaching-for-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/three-dimensional-wisdom-model> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-leadership> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/balance-theory-of-wisdom> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/balance-theory-of-wisdom/s1> .
