  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/teaching-for-wisdom/s6> <https://schema.org/url> <https://commons.emich.edu/fac_sch2018/85> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/teaching-for-wisdom/s7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/date> "2026-11-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/teaching-for-wisdom/s7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "JAMA Psychiatry, 77(9) (Lee, Bangen, Avanzino, Hou, Ramsey, Eglit, Liu, Tu, Paulus & Jeste, 2020; doi:10.1001/jamapsychiatry.2020.0821; eScholarship, University of California)" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/teaching-for-wisdom/s7> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Outcomes of randomized clinical trials of interventions to enhance social, emotional, and spiritual components of wisdom: A systematic review and meta-analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/teaching-for-wisdom/s7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Source> .
