<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What evidence would change my mind here, and have I actually gone looking for it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I holding the evidence that flatters me to the same standard as the evidence that doesn't?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who would tell me plainly how this looks from the outside, and have I asked them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If I turned out to be wrong about this, what would it cost me, and is that cost shaping what I see?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "If a peer had launched this and showed me these numbers, what would I tell them? I'll write down now what result would mean it isn't working, and ask two people who weren't involved to go through the data with me." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Those two never liked the change, and the numbers are just seasonal. It needs another quarter." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "Six months ago you championed a new onboarding process for your team. Completion rates are flat, and two team leads have told you that new hires find it confusing." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "The first response explains away each unwelcome fact on its own terms. The second fixes a standard before looking and borrows outside eyes, which makes it harder for a wish to steer how the evidence is read." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Obstacle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Self-deception" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "deceiving oneself" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "lying to oneself" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "self-deceit" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-knowledge> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Coming to believe, and keeping on believing, something one would prefer to be true in the face of evidence that points the other way, because desire, fear or self-regard biases how one seeks out, weighs and remembers that evidence; it is a leading obstacle to self-knowledge and to judging one's own conduct honestly." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/self-knowledge> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Self-deception" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/honesty> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/impartial-spectator> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-reflection> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-deception> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/theory-of-moral-sentiments> .
