  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/richard-lazarus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "American psychologist (1922–2002) at the University of California, Berkeley, whose cognitive appraisal theory held that stress and emotion depend on how a person judges what an event means for their goals and well-being; his film experiments and his work with Susan Folkman on coping are the source of reappraisal as a named way of changing how one feels." .
