  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/viktor-frankl> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Viennese neurologist and psychiatrist (1905–1997), Holocaust survivor and founder of logotherapy, whose account of the camps, Man's Search for Meaning, made the search for meaning a central idea in modern psychology and in popular thinking about how to live through suffering; historians and later research have questioned parts of his account and theory." .
