  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/vivian-clayton> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "American psychologist, later a geriatric neuropsychologist in California, whose 1970s graduate research is credited as the first attempt to study wisdom empirically; with James Birren she described wisdom as joining cognitive, reflective and affective (compassionate) qualities, and she distinguished wisdom, as judgment about whether to act, from intelligence, as skill at how to act." .
