<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What do I actually know here, and what am I only assuming or hoping?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What do I owe each person affected, including the people who are not in the room?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is fear of discomfort stopping me from doing what I already judge to be right?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is appetite, anger or the wish to look good pushing me past the right measure?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I leaning hard on one virtue, such as boldness or caution, at the expense of the others?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/check/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Check what the data actually support, raise the concern privately with the director first with the evidence and an honest alternative framing, and escalate calmly if it is ignored." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Either keep quiet because it isn't my call, or stand up in the board meeting and announce that the numbers are fudged." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "Your director asks you to present quarterly figures to the board with a forecast you believe is unrealistically rosy. Several colleagues' jobs depend on the board approving the plan." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Silence fails courage and justice, while a public outburst is courage without prudence or temperance. Asking all four questions together (what is true, what is owed, what must be faced, what is the right measure) produces a response that is honest, fair, brave and proportionate at once, which is the point of treating the virtues as a set." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Framework> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Cardinal virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "classical virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "four cardinal virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "principal virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "the four cardinal virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "virtutes cardinales" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/virtue-ethics> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The classical grouping of four virtues on which a good character was said to hinge: practical wisdom (prudence), justice, courage (fortitude) and temperance (moderation). First set out as the virtues of a well-ordered city and soul in Plato's Republic, it was taken up by the Stoics, Cicero and Christian moral theology, where it gained the name \"cardinal\", from the Latin cardo, hinge." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/virtues-and-character> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Cardinal virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/aristotle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/confucianism> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/cardinal-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/courage> .
