<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Before I settled on this view, did I actually look for the strongest case against it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I being careful and thorough here, or just quick and confident?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is my curiosity about this question real, or do I mainly want to be proved right?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Whose knowledge or testimony am I discounting, and is that because of the evidence or because of who they are?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-17"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Concept> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Intellectual virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "aretai dianoetikai" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "dianoetic virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "epistemic virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "intellectual character virtues" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "virtues of thought" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/virtue-ethics> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-virtues> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Excellences of the mind: the states and traits that make someone good at grasping truth and thinking well. Aristotle named five (craft, scientific knowledge, practical wisdom, intuitive reason and theoretical wisdom); modern virtue epistemology adds character traits of a good inquirer such as curiosity, open-mindedness, intellectual humility, intellectual courage, carefulness and tenacity." .
