<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I weighing my colleagues' advice as seriously as I would have before I had authority over them?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When nobody objected in that meeting, did I check whether they agreed or just stayed quiet?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Whose interests does this decision touch beyond the targets I am measured on?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I still doing the work myself because it is needed, or because it is where I feel competent?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Ask the colleague to walk the team through the design and its trade-offs, put the alternative on the table as one option rather than an order, ask who sees risks in either, and agree how the choice will be made and reviewed." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I'm the lead now, so we'll do it my way. I'll rewrite the plan tonight and hand out the tasks tomorrow." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A newly promoted team lead, formerly the team's strongest engineer, sees a colleague's design for a new service and is sure her own approach would be faster to build." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Relying on title wins compliance at best and silences the people closest to the work; inviting their view and weighing it treats authority as responsibility for the decision rather than a licence to skip other people's knowledge." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Context> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Leading others" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "becoming the boss" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "being a manager" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "having authority over others" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "leading a team" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "managing people" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/professional-work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The situation of being responsible for other people's work and growth — as a manager, team lead, coach or project head — where your decisions affect people who have less say than you, and where the power you hold can quietly change how well you listen and judge." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/wisdom-at-work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Leading others" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/after-action-review> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/egocentric-discounting> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/leading-others> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/hubris> .
