  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/stewardship/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Environmental Ethics (Brennan & Lo), Summer 2006 edition, sections 1-2" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/stewardship/s6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/stewardship/s6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#sourceType> "scholarly-encyclopedia" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/stewardship/s6> <https://schema.org/url> <https://plato.stanford.edu/archives/sum2006/entries/ethics-environmental/> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If I handed this role, team or budget to someone tomorrow, would it be in better or worse shape than when I received it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who will live with the consequences of this decision after I have moved on, and have I counted their interests?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I taking responsibility for this outcome, or quietly protecting my own record?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I calling it stewardship when I am really keeping control that others should share?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "Show my director what skipping the work would cost the team that inherits the system, propose a smaller feature set plus the essential fixes, and write a clear handover note either way." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Ship the features and skip the maintenance. The target is mine; the next team can deal with the debt." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "An engineering manager can hit this quarter's delivery target by skipping overdue maintenance on a system the team will hand over to another group next year." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "The first response treats the system as a means to one person's quarterly result. The stewardly response treats it as held in trust for its future users and owners, accepts a visible short-term cost, and is honest with the people who set the target." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-16"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Virtue> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Stewardship" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "being a good steward" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "oikonomia" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "steward leadership" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "stewardly leadership" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "trusteeship" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/moral-virtues> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-leadership> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The disposition to treat a role, a team, an institution or a resource as something held in trust for others, putting the long-term good of the people it serves (including those who will come later) ahead of one's own short-term gain, and taking personal responsibility for leaving it in better shape than one found it." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/wisdom-at-work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/stewardship> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Stewardship" .
