  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/confucianism> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The East Asian tradition of thought and practice that grew from the teaching of Confucius (Kong Qiu, 551–479 BCE), which holds that a good life and a good society come from lifelong learning and self-cultivation, expressed through humaneness (ren), ritual propriety (li), care for family and the example of the exemplary person (junzi)." .
