  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/epicureanism/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "The Classical Quarterly (Katharina Volk, 2025), Cambridge University Press, doi:10.1017/S0009838824000569" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/epicureanism/s6> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "Cicero and Epicurus on Pleasure and Friendship" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/epicureanism/s6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Source> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/epicureanism/s6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#sourceType> "peer-reviewed" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/epicureanism/s6> <https://schema.org/url> <https://core-cms.cambridgecore.org/core/services/aop-cambridge-core/content/view/86669298D590F2A08CF91B67D0F85BC2/S0009838824000569a.pdf/cicero-and-epicurus-on-pleasure-and-friendship.pdf> .
}

<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Can I be glad about this person's success, or am I quietly keeping score?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is what I am calling compassion here help for them, or my own distress at their pain?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Is my calm the steadiness of seeing clearly, or have I simply stopped caring?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Would I offer this same goodwill to someone I find difficult, or only to people on my side?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I let the disappointment register, then congratulate my peer properly and mean it. With the teammate I listen and ask what would help, without stoking the grievance, and I accept that the promotion decision is made and no longer mine to change." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I congratulate the winner through gritted teeth, then spend lunch with the other teammate agreeing that management is hopeless, and leave work feeling worse about both of them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A peer you trained wins the promotion you also applied for, on the same day another teammate tells you their project has just been cancelled." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Each person needed a different response; sympathetic joy keeps envy from souring the success, compassion meets the setback, and equanimity stops your own loss from colouring both." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Name the situation in front of you: someone is doing well, someone is suffering, someone is simply there, or the outcome is out of your hands." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Choose the quality that fits it, goodwill for the ordinary encounter, compassion for suffering, sympathetic joy for another's success and equanimity for what you cannot change." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Check the quality for its look-alike, asking whether goodwill has become clinging, compassion has become your own distress, joy has become excitement or calm has become not caring." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Widen the circle one step, offering the same attitude to someone neutral or difficult, not only to people you already like." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Afterwards, notice which of the four came easily and which you avoided, and practise the neglected one next time." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "The four immeasurables" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Framework> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The four immeasurables" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "appamaññā" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "apramāṇa" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "brahma-vihāra" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "brahmavihāras" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "divine abodes" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "four sublime states" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/buddhist-ethics> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Buddhist framework of four boundless attitudes toward all beings, loving-kindness (mettā), compassion (karuṇā), sympathetic joy (muditā) and equanimity (upekkhā), cultivated together so that each one corrects the typical failure of the others." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/wisdom-traditions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "The four immeasurables" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/four-immeasurables> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/empathy> .
